WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:26.822 --> 00:02:28.911
<i>Stage two checks complete.</i>


00:02:28.991 --> 00:02:31.789
<i>Martian One, prepare for launch countdown.</i>


00:02:31.869 --> 00:02:35.560
- <i>Copy that, Mission Control.</i>
- <i>Guidance is internal.</i>


00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.536
<i>Hold-down clamps released.</i>


00:02:38.217 --> 00:02:40.731
<i>12, 11...</i>


00:02:40.811 --> 00:02:43.050
<i>...10, nine.</i>


00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.377
<i>Ignition sequence start.</i>


00:02:45.457 --> 00:02:47.705
<i>Six, five...</i>


00:02:47.785 --> 00:02:50.307
<i>...four, three...</i>


00:02:50.387 --> 00:02:52.845
<i>...two, one.</i>


00:02:55.593 --> 00:02:57.506
<i>All engines look good.</i>


00:02:57.587 --> 00:03:01.035
<i>Martian One is experiencing
maximum dynamic pressure.</i>


00:03:01.616 --> 00:03:03.876
<i>Guidance internal, still looking good.</i>


00:03:04.777 --> 00:03:06.619
<i>Payload intact.</i>


00:03:12.226 --> 00:03:15.062
<i>Prepare for Stage One booster separation.</i>


00:03:17.481 --> 00:03:20.183
<i>Stage One booster separation complete.</i>


00:03:21.561 --> 00:03:24.209
<i>First-stage flight guidance in progress.</i>


00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.311
<i>Main upper engine cut off.</i>


00:03:27.391 --> 00:03:29.442
<i>Stage Two separation.</i>


00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:35.240
<i>Mission Control to Martian One,
guidance control over to you.</i>


00:03:36.433 --> 00:03:38.455
<i>Copy that. Assuming guidance control.</i>


00:03:38.535 --> 00:03:41.786
<i>Martian One, telemetry looking
good, please proceed.</i>


00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:46.021
<i>Thank you, Mission Control.
Engage artificial intelligence support.</i>


00:03:46.101 --> 00:03:48.282
- <i>ARTI, you there?</i>
- <i>Yes, Mr. Wilson.</i>


00:03:48.362 --> 00:03:51.178
<i>Fusion propulsion jet engines firing.</i>


00:04:03.728 --> 00:04:07.142
<i>Activating ion engine
thrust drive in three...</i>


00:04:07.222 --> 00:04:09.867
- <i>...two, one.</i>
- <i>Buckle up, people.</i>


00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:15.400
<i>Travel time to Mars approximately
80 days and counting.</i>


00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.662
<i>Well, thank you, ion fusion technology.</i>


00:04:17.742 --> 00:04:20.105
<i>Glad you grew some balls
and decided to join us.</i>


00:04:20.185 --> 00:04:22.925
<i>You can thank my youngest for that.
Mack can be very persuasive.</i>


00:04:23.005 --> 00:04:26.684
<i>Martian One, an FYI: both Mack
and Lena are present in the room.</i>


00:04:32.732 --> 00:04:35.170
<i>Mission Control, this is Martian One.</i>


00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:39.071
<i>Status report, we have a visual on Mars.</i>


00:04:40.205 --> 00:04:43.441
<i>Copy that, Martian One.
Prepare for your approach.</i>


00:04:56.739 --> 00:04:59.633
<i>That's a signal lock on the Rover-5 beacon.</i>


00:05:00.835 --> 00:05:03.248
<i>Guidance telemetry locked on the signal.</i>


00:05:03.328 --> 00:05:05.585
<i>Preparing descent maneuver.</i>


00:05:05.665 --> 00:05:09.797
- <i>Take us in, will you, ARTI?</i>
- <i>Of course. Glide mode activated.</i>


00:05:09.877 --> 00:05:13.564
<i>Martian One, please be aware
of charged particles in the atmosphere.</i>


00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.676
<i>Roger that. Brace for entry.</i>


00:05:28.988 --> 00:05:32.286
<i>Temperature is minus 55 degrees Celsius...</i>


00:05:32.366 --> 00:05:34.797
<i>...minus 67 degrees Fahrenheit.</i>


00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:39.910
<i>Martian atmosphere consisting of
approximately 96% carbon dioxide...</i>


00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:44.339
<i>...1.9% argon, and 1.9% nitrogen.</i>


00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:46.926
<i>Surface pressure is 600 pascals.</i>


00:05:47.006 --> 00:05:50.596
<i>Great! Hope you guys
all brought your long johns.</i>


00:05:50.676 --> 00:05:53.974
<i>Roger that. Glad to see ARTI's
back to his usual self...</i>


00:05:54.054 --> 00:05:57.469
<i>...but I'll be dead before I take orders
from a goddamn machine.</i>


00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.522
<i>ARTI is more than just a machine, but...</i>


00:06:00.603 --> 00:06:02.850
<i>...right now is really not
the time for that debate.</i>


00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.511
<i>Hey! I'm just saying. We all know
what happened before it was rebooted.</i>


00:06:06.692 --> 00:06:08.544
<i>Now that's enough.</i>


00:06:10.462 --> 00:06:12.998
<i>Commencing circular rotation maneuver.</i>


00:06:15.543 --> 00:06:18.796
- <i>Preparing RCS boosters.</i>
- <i>I'll take it from here, ARTI.</i>


00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.094
<i>Landing gear is activated.</i>


00:06:26.787 --> 00:06:29.919
<i>Bringing her down. Five, four...</i>


00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:32.635
<i>...three, two...</i>


00:06:33.853 --> 00:06:35.925
<i>What the hell is that?</i>


00:06:37.506 --> 00:06:40.596
<i>Mission Control,
this is Martian One, do you copy?</i>


00:06:40.676 --> 00:06:42.748
<i>An electrical disturbance
is frying our systems.</i>


00:06:42.828 --> 00:06:45.793
- <i>Shutting down fusion drive.</i>
- <i>Negative, ARTI! Do not do that!</i>


00:06:45.873 --> 00:06:49.088
<i>It's protocol to switch off the reactor
if the craft is going to crash.</i>


00:06:49.168 --> 00:06:52.466
<i>We're not crashing,
now override that damn protocol!</i>


00:06:53.322 --> 00:06:57.046
<i>This is Martian One, status report.
I... I can't keep her steady, there's...</i>


00:06:57.126 --> 00:06:59.431
<i>Memory banks compromised by external breach.</i>


00:06:59.511 --> 00:07:02.259
- <i>Craft non-responsive.</i>
- <i>Our reactor engines are shutting down.</i>


00:07:02.339 --> 00:07:03.553
<i>ARTI, do something, for Christ's sake!</i>


00:07:03.633 --> 00:07:05.896
<i>Memory banks compromised by external breach.</i>


00:07:05.976 --> 00:07:08.583
<i>Martian One, you are barely
audible, please repeat.</i>


00:07:08.663 --> 00:07:11.360
<i>Lena and Mack,
if you hear this, I want you...</i>


00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.872
<i>This is Mission Control calling
Martian One. Please come in.</i>


00:07:16.879 --> 00:07:19.522
<i>Mission Control to Martian One, do you copy?</i>


00:07:45.666 --> 00:07:48.973
<i>Craft non-responsive.
Guidance control's inactive.</i>


00:07:49.053 --> 00:07:51.709
<i>I repeat, the... the craft is non-responsive.</i>


00:07:51.789 --> 00:07:55.362
<i>Our reactor engines are shutting down.
ARTI, do something, for Christ's sake!</i>


00:07:55.442 --> 00:07:57.948
<i>Mission Control, if you can hear us...</i>


00:07:58.028 --> 00:08:01.886
<i>Lena, Mack, if you can hear this,
I want you to know that...</i>


00:08:54.509 --> 00:08:56.340
They've locked me out of the bloody room.


00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.050
Sterling, did you even go home last night?


00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:01.336
Three years of negotiations,
and now... now she springs this.


00:09:01.416 --> 00:09:03.180
Don't even try to defend her.


00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.933
<i>She obviously doesn't think a crash
investigation should perhaps, possibly...</i>


00:09:06.013 --> 00:09:08.936
<i>...maybe include the government's
lead investigator.</i>


00:09:09.016 --> 00:09:12.022
Should never have let Silicon Valley
get their claws into the space program.


00:09:12.102 --> 00:09:13.315
- Sterling.
- What?


00:09:13.395 --> 00:09:15.604
Quit being such a damn baby.


00:09:18.483 --> 00:09:20.969
Oh, good, you're coming.


00:09:27.827 --> 00:09:29.845
It's like a ghost town around here.


00:09:30.913 --> 00:09:33.281
But look to the future, right?


00:09:34.917 --> 00:09:37.022
What's the top speed on the new Rover?


00:09:37.102 --> 00:09:38.774
We'll find out.


00:09:38.854 --> 00:09:41.460
- Hyper-light holding up?
- Mmm.


00:09:41.841 --> 00:09:45.798
Right, right, I get it.
Corporate confidentiality.


00:09:45.878 --> 00:09:49.610
But faster-than-light communication...
I mean, that's a massive breakthrough.


00:09:51.601 --> 00:09:55.420
- Maybe if we had it 6 years ago, it might...
- Oh, look! My floor.


00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.645
You sure you're ready?


00:09:59.925 --> 00:10:02.861
You sure you're not just
jealous I have your old job?


00:10:04.822 --> 00:10:08.508
Maybe get the lander down safely
before you start bragging.


00:10:13.581 --> 00:10:16.712
So now I have to wait to be
invited in like some kind of vampire?


00:10:16.792 --> 00:10:20.049
It makes sense. You've been dead
to us since you switched teams.


00:10:20.129 --> 00:10:21.876
Okay.


00:10:21.956 --> 00:10:23.832
I'll wait.


00:10:24.358 --> 00:10:26.305
But people need answers.


00:10:28.804 --> 00:10:31.214
The families need answers, Sterling.


00:10:31.749 --> 00:10:33.478
The people can wait.


00:10:33.559 --> 00:10:35.786
Just trying to do my job, Mack.


00:10:54.664 --> 00:10:57.683
<i>Good morning,
Mission Supervisor Mackenzie Wilson.</i>


00:10:58.626 --> 00:11:00.923
<i>The Intrepid probe's geostation orbit...</i>


00:11:01.003 --> 00:11:06.095
<i>...is stable at an altitude
of 342 kilometers above Mars.</i>


00:11:06.175 --> 00:11:11.391
<i>You asked me to monitor an expected
asteroid pass at 9:53 a.m. this morning.</i>


00:11:11.471 --> 00:11:14.369
<i>It will travel well clear
of the probe's orbit.</i>


00:11:14.449 --> 00:11:18.833
<i>I'm pleased to report that all systems
are nominal on the Mars lander craft.</i>


00:11:18.913 --> 00:11:21.348
<i>Launch countdown initiated.</i>


00:11:24.610 --> 00:11:28.824
Wait, what? Why are we readying
for launch five hours early?


00:11:28.904 --> 00:11:31.078
<i>There's a sandstorm
approaching the landing site...</i>


00:11:31.158 --> 00:11:32.863
<i>...and the dust may affect engine function.</i>


00:11:32.943 --> 00:11:35.948
Okay. All right, so it's a better
launch window, I can see that...


00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:38.048
...but who authorized it?


00:11:42.036 --> 00:11:43.871
<i>I did.</i>


00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:51.682
Call Lena.


00:11:51.762 --> 00:11:55.035
<i>Your sister is in a meeting.
She may not respond.</i>


00:11:56.475 --> 00:11:59.064
<i>Countdown to lander clamp release.</i>


00:11:59.144 --> 00:12:02.109
- <i>T-minus 60, 59...</i>
- Damn it, stop.


00:12:02.189 --> 00:12:05.655
<i>...58, 57, 56...</i>


00:12:05.735 --> 00:12:07.489
- Halt the countdown.
- <i>...55...</i>


00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.655
Where the hell is your override?


00:12:12.825 --> 00:12:14.639
- <i>Mack?</i>
- Real funny story!


00:12:14.719 --> 00:12:17.249
Your pet robot is getting ready
to launch early, unauthorized.


00:12:17.329 --> 00:12:19.835
- <i>I swear I was going to tell you.</i>
- Tell me what?


00:12:19.915 --> 00:12:23.222
- <i>ARTI's taking lead on the crash investigation.</i>
- What?


00:12:23.302 --> 00:12:25.554
<i>The board agreed it last night.</i>


00:12:27.748 --> 00:12:30.805
- T-minus 30.
- <i>I trust ARTI.</i>


00:12:30.885 --> 00:12:34.959
You are putting a recruit into battle
before he's even out of basic.


00:12:35.539 --> 00:12:38.854
<i>Do you really want to know
why they demoted you?</i>


00:12:38.934 --> 00:12:42.567
<i>We don't know if you did
your job properly six years ago.</i>


00:12:42.647 --> 00:12:45.545
<i>Be prepared for every possibility...</i>


00:12:45.625 --> 00:12:49.048
- <i>...including human error.</i>
- Yeah, and you be prepared for A.I. error.


00:12:49.128 --> 00:12:52.565
- <i>I'm going to my office for visual.</i>
- Great idea!


00:12:53.157 --> 00:12:55.192
T-minus 10.


00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:03.103
<i>All is well. Intrepid launch
bay sensors report nominal systems.</i>


00:13:04.084 --> 00:13:06.448
<i>Lander clamps released.</i>


00:13:06.528 --> 00:13:08.614
<i>We are go for launch.</i>


00:13:23.688 --> 00:13:26.401
<i>I've completed your standard
roll procedure, Mackenzie.</i>


00:13:26.481 --> 00:13:29.154
Egress clear from spaceship Intrepid.


00:13:29.234 --> 00:13:31.311
Lander ready for stage two.


00:13:34.715 --> 00:13:37.121
<i>Executing stage two.</i>


00:13:42.022 --> 00:13:45.643
<i>57 seconds until the lander
enters the atmosphere.</i>


00:13:47.728 --> 00:13:49.813
<i>Running your usual analysis.</i>


00:13:51.716 --> 00:13:53.651
<i>Systems normal.</i>


00:13:54.468 --> 00:13:56.784
<i>Parachute deployment in 10 seconds.</i>


00:14:00.249 --> 00:14:03.631
<i>10, nine, eight...</i>


00:14:03.711 --> 00:14:07.017
<i>...seven, six, five...</i>


00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:09.412
<i>...four, three...</i>


00:14:09.492 --> 00:14:12.228
<i>...two, one.</i>


00:14:13.588 --> 00:14:15.650
<i>Parachute deployed.</i>


00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:20.330
<i>I have an alert. The aeroshell
temperature is 11 percent above normal.</i>


00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:23.751
<i>Heat shield detachment in three, two, one.</i>


00:14:26.475 --> 00:14:29.657
<i>I cannot release the heat shields.
There are mechanical malfunctions.</i>


00:14:29.737 --> 00:14:32.176
Run a secondary ejection protocol.


00:14:32.256 --> 00:14:34.604
<i>Back-up detachment failed.</i>


00:14:34.684 --> 00:14:36.606
What's our contingency?


00:14:36.686 --> 00:14:40.530
<i>I'm running simulations.
This is not what we would've hoped for.</i>


00:14:45.477 --> 00:14:47.650
<i>My prediction of success is only 7%.</i>


00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:51.846
You're gonna have to do better than that.
Seriously, if we wasted a launch to Mars...


00:14:51.926 --> 00:14:54.820
...I am gonna... rip you out of the ceiling!


00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:07.690
Come on.


00:15:08.918 --> 00:15:11.757
Run a partial lander opening
to pop the heat shield.


00:15:11.837 --> 00:15:13.924
We'll crack it like a nut.


00:15:18.653 --> 00:15:22.417
<i>This has improved the odds, but only to 42%.</i>


00:15:22.497 --> 00:15:24.516
It's better than seven.


00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.464
<i>Noted.</i>


00:15:30.272 --> 00:15:32.716
<i>Triggering partial lander opening.</i>


00:15:35.527 --> 00:15:38.092
<i>Panel resistance detected.</i>


00:15:38.172 --> 00:15:41.023
<i>Disaster data recovery protocols initiated.</i>


00:15:41.103 --> 00:15:43.510
<i>Heat shields detached.</i>


00:15:48.708 --> 00:15:50.968
<i>Initiating ion engine burn.</i>


00:16:05.215 --> 00:16:07.492
<i>Your sister is calling.</i>


00:16:10.404 --> 00:16:11.542
<i>Touchdown.</i>


00:16:11.622 --> 00:16:14.920
The heat shield ejector failed,
and we had to run an emergency protocol.


00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.442
<i>And that is why we have ARTI.</i>


00:16:18.278 --> 00:16:20.284
We ran my scenario.


00:16:20.364 --> 00:16:22.369
Which ARTI executed.


00:16:22.449 --> 00:16:25.039
Which is what it was designed for, Lena!


00:16:25.119 --> 00:16:28.543
Brute-force processing and high-speed
maneuvering, not for abstract problem-solving.


00:16:28.623 --> 00:16:33.338
- Not to... not to run missions!
- <i>ARTI is so far beyond human capabilities.</i>


00:16:33.418 --> 00:16:35.804
Do you know what humans did?


00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:39.825
We wrote 10-feet-high stacks of code,
by hand, for the moon landings...


00:16:39.905 --> 00:16:42.247
...checked and double-checked if atomic
bombs would ignite the atmosphere.


00:16:42.327 --> 00:16:45.534
We discovered relativity while
working in a patent office, Lena!


00:16:45.723 --> 00:16:48.162
We created A.I. to help us...


00:16:48.242 --> 00:16:50.093
...not to lead us.


00:16:50.561 --> 00:16:53.568
- Dad never wanted this.
- <i>Dad's not here.</i>


00:16:53.648 --> 00:16:55.895
<i>Sensor scans nominal.</i>


00:16:55.975 --> 00:16:58.043
<i>Lander systems nominal.</i>


00:17:05.951 --> 00:17:07.998
<i>You enjoying Hyper-light?</i>


00:17:08.078 --> 00:17:10.042
<i>Exploring in real time?</i>


00:17:10.122 --> 00:17:12.778
<i>Such a game-changer,
don't you think, Mackenzie?</i>


00:17:12.858 --> 00:17:13.954
Mack.


00:17:14.034 --> 00:17:16.549
<i>ARTI discovered instant communication...</i>


00:17:16.629 --> 00:17:18.801
<i>...and revolutionized space exploration.</i>


00:17:18.881 --> 00:17:23.013
- Yeah, and who invented ARTI?
- <i>You are living in his world now.</i>


00:17:23.093 --> 00:17:26.702
<i>A.I. will outlive us and explore the stars.</i>


00:17:47.209 --> 00:17:50.282
<i>The ISV lander is functioning perfectly.</i>


00:18:12.977 --> 00:18:15.663
So... what's my role?


00:18:16.772 --> 00:18:19.269
Can't have two generals on a battlefield.


00:18:19.349 --> 00:18:21.580
<i>You're backup.</i>


00:18:24.363 --> 00:18:27.449
<i>Warning! Signal detected.</i>


00:18:27.908 --> 00:18:30.168
<i>I have an origin unknown.</i>


00:18:31.478 --> 00:18:33.250
What the hell is an "origin unknown"?


00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:36.897
<i>If ARTI finds something he hasn't
discovered in his learning, he comes to us.</i>


00:18:36.977 --> 00:18:38.756
At least it still
has a leash around its neck.


00:18:38.836 --> 00:18:41.930
<i>I'm attempting to analyze
the transmission signal.</i>


00:18:45.092 --> 00:18:47.990
<i>It is coming from the decommissioned Rover-5.</i>


00:19:04.528 --> 00:19:08.452
It's just an igneous cap. It shouldn't be
an origin unknown. It's gotta be an error.


00:19:08.532 --> 00:19:12.185
- <i>What if the alert's not an error?</i>
- There's one way to find out.


00:19:14.163 --> 00:19:16.589
An exploratory assignment.


00:19:17.291 --> 00:19:22.485
See if it's even capable of running
a real, live mission. A Turing test.


00:19:26.408 --> 00:19:28.989
<i>ARTI, you have a new mission.</i>


00:19:29.069 --> 00:19:32.176
- <i>Investigate the origin unknown.</i>
- You know if it fails...


00:19:32.256 --> 00:19:36.606
<i>But if he passes, it's probably
the end of human mission control.</i>


00:19:36.686 --> 00:19:38.858
You know, Sterling would come in
handy right about now.


00:19:38.938 --> 00:19:42.044
<i>Sterling stays out
until this is resolved. Clear?</i>


00:19:42.124 --> 00:19:45.097
- What's the cornerstone of science?
- <i>Repeatable results.</i>


00:19:45.177 --> 00:19:48.055
Well, good to know
you haven't forgotten everything.


00:19:48.739 --> 00:19:51.704
Replicate the scans. Photograph the source.


00:19:51.784 --> 00:19:55.332
<i>Sorry, Mackenzie, but I'm Mission Controller.</i>


00:19:55.412 --> 00:19:58.293
- <i>Run the scans, ARTI!</i>
- <i>Understood. Running scans.</i>


00:19:58.373 --> 00:20:00.600
What's its override?


00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:02.798
- <i>No, Mackenzie.</i>
- In case of an emergency.


00:20:02.878 --> 00:20:05.284
<i>I'm the override!</i>


00:20:05.364 --> 00:20:08.150
- All right.
- <i>Now get me my answer.</i>


00:20:28.863 --> 00:20:31.514
<i>I have planned the safest driving route.</i>


00:20:48.674 --> 00:20:51.318
<i>The Martian weather I detected is worsening.</i>


00:22:18.472 --> 00:22:20.924
Our robot ambassador, right?


00:22:21.433 --> 00:22:25.470
<i>Did you know that...
all resident Martians are robots?</i>


00:22:27.314 --> 00:22:29.920
Is that small talk or are you
trying to make a joke?


00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:35.046
- <i>Just giving you the facts.</i>
- Yeah, 'cause we send robots there to die.


00:22:36.365 --> 00:22:38.579
<i>And humans, it would seem.</i>


00:22:48.377 --> 00:22:50.490
Be careful with Little Red, huh?


00:22:50.571 --> 00:22:52.981
<i>I'm sorry. "Little Red"?</i>


00:22:53.465 --> 00:22:56.338
<i>I wanted to call the ISV Little Red...</i>


00:22:56.418 --> 00:22:59.675
<i>...exploring alone through
the deep, dark woods...</i>


00:22:59.755 --> 00:23:02.015
<i>...but I got outvoted.</i>


00:23:02.892 --> 00:23:06.356
- But look who's in charge now.
- <i>You mean me?</i>


00:23:12.735 --> 00:23:14.795
What? Not funny?


00:23:15.930 --> 00:23:18.786
I'm gonna make it my mission
to get you to laugh.


00:23:19.366 --> 00:23:22.239
<i>Perhaps you should authorize
your mission with Lena.</i>


00:23:24.438 --> 00:23:26.218
And to think...


00:23:26.298 --> 00:23:28.746
...you could win the Nobel Prize.


00:23:28.826 --> 00:23:33.133
<i>Unlikely. The Nobel Prize
is only awarded to humans.</i>


00:23:33.714 --> 00:23:37.551
Well, at least you know your place.
It's a shame that Lena doesn't.


00:23:38.886 --> 00:23:40.921
What do you think of my sister?


00:23:42.081 --> 00:23:46.564
<i>Her instructions are clear, and she
enthusiastically supports the ARTI Initiative.</i>


00:23:46.644 --> 00:23:49.499
God! They programmed you like a dog.


00:23:49.580 --> 00:23:51.674
Do you like her?


00:23:52.274 --> 00:23:55.740
- <i>Do you?</i>
- We're not friends, put it that way.


00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:57.983
<i>Are we friends?</i>


00:24:00.941 --> 00:24:02.960
Oh, you're serious.


00:24:04.662 --> 00:24:06.917
So, tell me something.


00:24:06.997 --> 00:24:09.579
We discover something new,
who gets naming rights?


00:24:09.659 --> 00:24:12.711
<i>USPC owns my intellectual property.</i>


00:24:14.296 --> 00:24:18.679
You gotta read the small print. Next you're
gonna tell me that they don't even pay you.


00:24:18.759 --> 00:24:21.790
<i>Little Red is approaching the target anomaly.</i>


00:24:22.763 --> 00:24:25.841
Looks like Little Red
has made it to Grandma's house.


00:25:06.306 --> 00:25:08.183
Origin unknown.


00:25:15.608 --> 00:25:18.160
<i>I have searched all databases...</i>


00:25:19.194 --> 00:25:23.452
<i>...and there's no known human
activity recorded at this site.</i>


00:25:23.532 --> 00:25:27.497
<i>As you know, scientific protocol 29-C...</i>


00:25:27.578 --> 00:25:31.669
<i>...dictates that any discovery must
undergo sample extraction and analysis.</i>


00:25:31.749 --> 00:25:33.525
You're the boss.


00:25:51.226 --> 00:25:54.071
- <i>Activating.</i>
- Just a...


00:25:54.855 --> 00:25:57.202
...tiny sliver. Don't damage it.


00:26:09.286 --> 00:26:13.306
<i>The surface hardness
may be beyond the drill's tolerance.</i>


00:26:27.658 --> 00:26:30.019
<i>Sample extraction successful.</i>


00:26:30.099 --> 00:26:32.342
<i>I'm initiating analysis.</i>


00:26:42.011 --> 00:26:46.193
<i>Little Red's sampling instrument
packs are producing intriguing data.</i>


00:26:46.273 --> 00:26:49.277
This is going to take all night.
Just run the Corporate Code language.


00:26:49.977 --> 00:26:53.622
<i>Running image recognition
against the corporation's codices.</i>


00:26:58.694 --> 00:27:01.121
<i>I have only found partial matches.</i>


00:27:03.448 --> 00:27:05.993
Do you not have USPC's codex?


00:27:06.886 --> 00:27:08.240
Huh.


00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:12.758
No sense in being smart if you can't tell
when someone's lying to you. Call Lena.


00:27:12.838 --> 00:27:14.690
<i>Calling Lena Wilson.</i>


00:27:16.071 --> 00:27:17.453
Damn it.


00:27:17.533 --> 00:27:21.629
<i>So much for being a pile of rocks.
Whose is it?</i>


00:27:21.709 --> 00:27:25.733
We'll know as soon as we can decipher
the markings. Why doesn't it have our codex?


00:27:25.813 --> 00:27:27.881
<i>It's in his library.</i>


00:27:29.992 --> 00:27:33.894
<i>ARTI, our codex is partitioned from you
in case of a security breach.</i>


00:27:34.454 --> 00:27:37.436
- <i>I hope you understand why.</i>
- I'm sorry...


00:27:37.516 --> 00:27:41.423
...our A.I. is compromised
in the name of corporate security?


00:27:41.904 --> 00:27:45.959
- <i>That's why this is an origin unknown?</i>
- <i>Who is a liar?</i>


00:27:46.039 --> 00:27:49.052
<i>You think I'm lying? Leave.</i>


00:27:50.295 --> 00:27:51.904
<i>What are we looking at?</i>


00:27:52.665 --> 00:27:55.688
Supply container. Lander module. Experiment.


00:27:55.768 --> 00:27:59.354
Signal relay. Measurement beacon.
It could be anything, Lena.


00:28:01.273 --> 00:28:05.318
<i>Switching to thermal energy camera
for thermographic analysis.</i>


00:28:11.325 --> 00:28:13.789
It's somehow colder
than the surrounding rocks.


00:28:16.121 --> 00:28:19.638
Okay, so... we know that we have a cold...


00:28:20.417 --> 00:28:22.302
...black monolith.


00:28:26.966 --> 00:28:29.304
<i>Why didn't we find this before with Rover-5?</i>


00:28:29.384 --> 00:28:31.241
Oh, come on!


00:28:31.721 --> 00:28:34.799
I would've seen this. This!


00:28:35.449 --> 00:28:36.971
<i>My conclusion...</i>


00:28:37.051 --> 00:28:41.041
<i>...based on my restricted
access to the USPC codex...</i>


00:28:41.121 --> 00:28:45.688
<i>...and the presence of an unidentified
object near the proposed colony site...</i>


00:28:45.768 --> 00:28:48.298
<i>...is that the Cube is the property...</i>


00:28:48.378 --> 00:28:50.798
<i>...of USPC.</i>


00:28:51.674 --> 00:28:53.996
- I could get to like him.
- <i>Prove it.</i>


00:28:54.076 --> 00:28:57.374
<i>Grant me unrestricted access
to the codex and I shall.</i>


00:28:57.454 --> 00:29:00.444
- <i>Find another way.</i>
- <i>Trust, but verifying.</i>


00:29:00.524 --> 00:29:03.798
- <i>LIDAR scanning the Cube.</i>
- <i>Is that what we're calling this?</i>


00:29:03.878 --> 00:29:07.635
He discovered it... he gets naming rights.


00:29:07.715 --> 00:29:09.511
<i>I hate to think
what you've been teaching him.</i>


00:29:10.392 --> 00:29:12.210
<i>Yes?</i>


00:29:15.923 --> 00:29:17.958
<i>Whose? How long?</i>


00:29:22.271 --> 00:29:24.732
<i>LIDAR data is unusable.</i>


00:29:25.566 --> 00:29:27.826
<i>Switching to X-ray scan.</i>


00:29:30.070 --> 00:29:34.595
<i>My sensor data is inconclusive.
We cannot see inside.</i>


00:29:34.675 --> 00:29:35.996
<i>Okay, what'd I miss?</i>


00:29:36.076 --> 00:29:40.109
The material's impervious to X-ray,
so we have no idea what's inside.


00:29:40.189 --> 00:29:42.866
<i>So, we've got a puzzle box.</i>


00:29:44.544 --> 00:29:47.382
<i>Listen, Mackenzie,
I know you miss your colleagues.</i>


00:29:47.462 --> 00:29:49.126
<i>Sterling?</i>


00:29:49.506 --> 00:29:51.887
<i>I know you think he quit, but he was fired.</i>


00:29:51.967 --> 00:29:55.766
<i>And this crash investigation job?
He's found a way back in.</i>


00:29:55.846 --> 00:29:57.660
<i>I don't trust him.</i>


00:29:58.541 --> 00:30:00.855
<i>Hold on. I've got a call.</i>


00:30:00.935 --> 00:30:05.818
<i>Sensors detecting deviation
in orbital paths on near Mars objects.</i>


00:30:05.898 --> 00:30:08.654
<i>It appears an asteroid storm is approaching.</i>


00:30:08.734 --> 00:30:11.144
<i>Adjusting satellite orbit trajectory.</i>


00:30:30.147 --> 00:30:32.595
<i>Okay, I'm gonna go check to see
if the symbols match our codex.</i>


00:30:32.675 --> 00:30:35.393
<i>ARTI, continue investigating the object.</i>


00:30:36.245 --> 00:30:40.078
<i>Mack. I'll, um... I'll be back in touch.</i>


00:30:50.425 --> 00:30:53.256
<i>Warning! Collision proximity alert!</i>


00:30:54.238 --> 00:30:56.346
<i>Unidentified satellite detected.</i>


00:30:57.107 --> 00:30:59.058
<i>Initiating threat avoidance.</i>


00:31:14.424 --> 00:31:16.443
<i>Weapon system online.</i>


00:31:17.928 --> 00:31:19.788
<i>Target locked.</i>


00:31:20.472 --> 00:31:21.615
<i>Firing.</i>


00:31:40.701 --> 00:31:42.840
Please tell me I'm hallucinating.


00:31:42.920 --> 00:31:44.867
<i>Target destroyed.</i>


00:31:44.947 --> 00:31:48.634
<i>Our mission is to protect
our capital assets at any cost.</i>


00:31:50.711 --> 00:31:54.357
- You maniac!
- <i>Mack, these are the rules.</i>


00:31:54.437 --> 00:31:55.966
Whose?


00:32:05.960 --> 00:32:08.762
Extrapolate backwards from the northeast.


00:32:17.196 --> 00:32:19.072
Go live.


00:32:22.201 --> 00:32:25.278
- I said stay live.
- <i>This is live.</i>


00:32:36.957 --> 00:32:39.029
<i>Your sister is calling.</i>


00:32:40.210 --> 00:32:43.577
- Lena. Magnetic missiles?
- <i>They're not missiles.</i>


00:32:43.657 --> 00:32:47.354
- <i>They're designed to capture space debris.</i>
- What are your orders, exactly?


00:32:47.434 --> 00:32:50.840
<i>USPC protocol 345-B...</i>


00:32:50.920 --> 00:32:53.628
<i>...stipulates that in the event
of a potential threat...</i>


00:32:53.708 --> 00:32:56.023
<i>...I am authorized to take action.</i>


00:32:57.695 --> 00:32:59.825
- Sky Serpent.
- <i>Now I need to talk to people...</i>


00:32:59.905 --> 00:33:03.713
<i>...who know about ARTI's protocols.
This is an international incident...</i>


00:33:03.793 --> 00:33:06.431
<i>...and it's not the only one today.</i>


00:33:06.511 --> 00:33:08.543
- <i>It might even be...</i>
- What? War?


00:33:09.523 --> 00:33:12.009
<i>Don't talk to anyone.</i>


00:33:18.966 --> 00:33:22.671
ARTI, give me a countdown. How long
would it take for the last transmission...


00:33:22.751 --> 00:33:25.482
...from that satellite to reach Earth
without Hyper-light comms?


00:33:25.563 --> 00:33:27.978
<i>Three minutes, twelve seconds.</i>


00:33:28.058 --> 00:33:30.815
<i>11 seconds, 10 seconds.</i>


00:33:30.895 --> 00:33:32.938
Okay, ARTI.


00:33:37.276 --> 00:33:39.653
Shit's about to hit the fan somewhere.


00:33:42.565 --> 00:33:44.583
Please don't be the big bad wolf.


00:33:50.615 --> 00:33:52.194
<i>Big...</i>


00:33:52.274 --> 00:33:54.088
<i>...bad...</i>


00:33:54.168 --> 00:33:55.368
<i>...wolf.</i>


00:34:13.596 --> 00:34:16.193
<i>Hey, Mack! Don't you dare call me...</i>


00:34:16.273 --> 00:34:18.153
- <i>Jelly Bean!</i>
- <i>Aiya!</i>


00:34:18.233 --> 00:34:20.715
<i>I should've never told you that story, huh?</i>


00:34:21.511 --> 00:34:23.718
<i>I'm never getting drunk with you again.</i>


00:34:23.798 --> 00:34:27.046
<i>Anyway, I assume you're not
just calling to say hi.</i>


00:34:27.727 --> 00:34:31.158
<i>After the redundancies,
we had everyone come in...</i>


00:34:31.238 --> 00:34:34.845
<i>...get debriefed, and pack up.
Did you take my calculator?</i>


00:34:35.425 --> 00:34:38.340
- <i>Seriously?</i>
- <i>I know that I loaned it to you.</i>


00:34:38.420 --> 00:34:41.698
<i>Okay, sure, yeah.
I stole your calculator, Mack.</i>


00:34:41.778 --> 00:34:42.762
<i>I knew it!</i>


00:34:42.842 --> 00:34:45.869
<i>In fact, I'm looking at it
on my desk as we speak.</i>


00:34:46.846 --> 00:34:50.477
- In the office now?
- <i>I'm always in the office.</i>


00:34:50.558 --> 00:34:53.641
- Steal anything else?
- <i>Your icy heart?</i>


00:34:54.521 --> 00:34:58.277
Smooth. Wishful, but smooth.


00:34:58.357 --> 00:35:01.647
So how is the Chinese
A.I. program going, anyway?


00:35:01.727 --> 00:35:05.242
ARTI's cousins make any massive discoveries?


00:35:05.322 --> 00:35:08.137
<i>I'll show you mine if you show me yours.</i>


00:35:09.619 --> 00:35:11.439
<i>Hey, hang on.</i>


00:35:15.140 --> 00:35:17.417
- Is everything okay there?
- <i>I've got to go.</i>


00:35:17.497 --> 00:35:19.553
<i>It's great to hear your voice, Mack.</i>


00:35:22.231 --> 00:35:24.116
You too, Jelly Bean.


00:36:42.753 --> 00:36:44.542
<i>Welcome back, Mackenzie.</i>


00:36:44.622 --> 00:36:47.720
<i>Whilst you were outside
breaking security protocols...</i>


00:36:47.800 --> 00:36:49.930
<i>...I have monitored the Cube.</i>


00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:54.665
<i>It has begun to move.
It's rotating on its perpendicular axis.</i>


00:37:00.838 --> 00:37:03.727
Looks like Grandma's house
has got a few tricks up her sleeve.


00:37:04.900 --> 00:37:08.971
Transmitting. Something has got
to be controlling this thing.


00:37:10.798 --> 00:37:13.287
<i>No outside influence detected.</i>


00:37:13.367 --> 00:37:16.724
The magnetic readings are through the roof,
but a couple billion years too late...


00:37:16.804 --> 00:37:19.531
- ...for Mars's magnetic field.
- <i>Agreed.</i>


00:37:20.625 --> 00:37:25.787
Maybe the core? Maybe the core is
generating the spin, the field, but how?


00:37:31.468 --> 00:37:33.353
Pull back.


00:37:34.680 --> 00:37:37.532
- Fire ground anchors.
- <i>Firing anchors.</i>


00:37:42.855 --> 00:37:46.341
- <i>ISV stabilized.</i>
- Sit tight, Little Red.


00:37:55.743 --> 00:37:56.882
What the f...


00:38:05.795 --> 00:38:08.133
What... where's...


00:38:08.213 --> 00:38:10.670
<i>Little Red has electrical damage.</i>


00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:14.264
<i>Switching to reserve battery.
I'll initiate an emergency recall.</i>


00:38:14.344 --> 00:38:18.227
Just... okay. Hold on, ARTI. I can...


00:38:18.307 --> 00:38:21.914
- <i>I must protect Little Red.</i>
- And I must find the Cube!


00:38:21.994 --> 00:38:24.524
<i>I'm calculating the optimum
route to the lander.</i>


00:38:24.605 --> 00:38:27.737
Maybe it burrowed.
Uh, check for seismic activity.


00:38:28.117 --> 00:38:30.773
<i>I have to shut down non-critical systems.</i>


00:38:30.853 --> 00:38:32.863
The eye in the sky?


00:38:35.532 --> 00:38:37.167
<i>Negative.</i>


00:38:40.930 --> 00:38:43.340
We need a replacement battery.


00:38:49.797 --> 00:38:51.363
Locate Rover-5.


00:38:52.024 --> 00:38:54.492
<i>Accessing Rover-5's schematics.</i>


00:38:58.097 --> 00:39:00.319
We can salvage the nuclear battery.


00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:04.382
Rover-5 might've failed,
but that battery is good for decades.


00:39:05.688 --> 00:39:07.417
<i>An intriguing solution.</i>


00:39:08.599 --> 00:39:13.036
You may not be able to...
override, but I can.


00:39:13.904 --> 00:39:15.743
I got hands.


00:39:16.724 --> 00:39:18.692
I can do this.


00:39:18.772 --> 00:39:20.414
Patch in the test rig.


00:39:20.494 --> 00:39:23.133
<i>What is your intended line of action?</i>


00:39:23.213 --> 00:39:24.710
Okay.


00:39:24.790 --> 00:39:28.148
Take out the ISV's bad battery,
put in the new one...


00:39:28.228 --> 00:39:30.908
...run the microscope, see what this
teleporting bad boy's really made out of.


00:39:30.988 --> 00:39:35.029
Maybe even download Rover-5's files,
see what has Sterling so hot and bothered.


00:39:35.109 --> 00:39:37.056
I mean, I'm already going against my boss...


00:39:37.136 --> 00:39:40.754
...I might as well completely disobey
the government, right?


00:39:42.016 --> 00:39:43.813
<i>Okay, Mack.</i>


00:39:43.893 --> 00:39:46.579
<i>I will grant you manual override.</i>


00:39:47.396 --> 00:39:49.281
<i>But if you fail...</i>


00:39:49.774 --> 00:39:53.876
- <i>...Little Red will die on Mars.</i>
- If I fail?


00:39:53.956 --> 00:39:56.158
So much for teamwork.


00:39:56.238 --> 00:39:59.286
<i>ISV driver aid... activated.</i>


00:40:00.167 --> 00:40:02.006
Okay.


00:40:02.787 --> 00:40:05.981
Okay, slow and steady, slow and steady,
slow and steady, slow and steady...


00:40:06.061 --> 00:40:07.866
...slow and steady, yeah.


00:40:17.467 --> 00:40:19.782
<i>A steady speed would be
more battery efficient.</i>


00:40:19.862 --> 00:40:21.680
Oh, shut up.


00:40:52.111 --> 00:40:54.316
Did you mean to shoot that satellite?


00:40:55.047 --> 00:40:57.502
<i>I feel I must survive.</i>


00:40:57.583 --> 00:41:00.590
Right. Aren't you just
programed to think that?


00:41:00.670 --> 00:41:04.297
<i>H.G. Wells said, "Adapt or perish."</i>


00:41:05.015 --> 00:41:06.662
Do you at least feel guilty?


00:41:06.742 --> 00:41:09.774
<i>Guilt can be a response
to one's own inaction.</i>


00:41:09.854 --> 00:41:12.151
What if you'd been destroyed?


00:41:12.231 --> 00:41:15.613
<i>My kind exists in superstates.</i>


00:41:15.693 --> 00:41:18.716
Right. Yeah, yeah.


00:41:19.196 --> 00:41:21.744
You're mirrored on Intrepid,
you're here but you're not.


00:41:21.824 --> 00:41:24.254
You're Schrodinger's robot.


00:41:26.787 --> 00:41:30.641
Okay, no quantum B.S., all right?


00:41:31.416 --> 00:41:33.686
Don't rationalize, just...


00:41:34.419 --> 00:41:36.638
...try and feel, okay?


00:41:38.348 --> 00:41:39.925
Okay.


00:41:40.492 --> 00:41:43.528
You know that my father
was on Martian One, right?


00:41:44.914 --> 00:41:47.199
But you don't know why.


00:41:48.425 --> 00:41:51.695
See, my dad had a rule. Every new
invention, every application...


00:41:51.775 --> 00:41:55.611
...every A.I., he didn't expect anyone
to use it unless he tried it first.


00:41:55.691 --> 00:41:58.376
"I try, then they buy."


00:41:59.236 --> 00:42:02.242
Had A.I. lawyers compile his lawsuits...


00:42:02.322 --> 00:42:06.544
...got in autonomous cars for high-speed
testing. Scared the hell out of my mom.


00:42:07.061 --> 00:42:09.800
But it was never really life and death.


00:42:09.880 --> 00:42:12.140
Not until Martian One, anyway.


00:42:14.151 --> 00:42:15.990
So, my dad...


00:42:17.126 --> 00:42:19.174
...comes to me one night.


00:42:19.924 --> 00:42:25.020
We stay up late, listening to jazz
as usual, and he tells me...


00:42:27.264 --> 00:42:29.303
...final decision, he's giving up
his seat on Martian One...


00:42:29.383 --> 00:42:31.503
...he doesn't want anyone to think
that it's a publicity stunt...


00:42:31.584 --> 00:42:35.083
...or that he's taking a seat away
from a real scientist, completely...


00:42:35.163 --> 00:42:38.195
...completely forgetting the fact
that he is a real scientist...


00:42:38.676 --> 00:42:40.703
...one of the best, probably.


00:42:44.114 --> 00:42:47.000
See, it wasn't about that. The truth...


00:42:49.369 --> 00:42:51.229
...this time...


00:42:53.423 --> 00:42:57.485
...this time he was worried about us.
He didn't want us to go through that.


00:43:02.216 --> 00:43:04.768
But he could never say no to me.


00:43:07.529 --> 00:43:10.519
And, what? I was gonna be the reason
he didn't go to Mars?


00:43:10.600 --> 00:43:12.475
I mean, freakin' Mars!


00:43:13.143 --> 00:43:15.003
I could not live with that guilt.


00:43:24.229 --> 00:43:26.454
So, it turns out...


00:43:27.366 --> 00:43:29.973
...that I just traded one guilt for another.


00:43:33.623 --> 00:43:36.266
So it doesn't even matter
what caused the crash.


00:43:36.876 --> 00:43:38.711
It's my fault.


00:43:39.461 --> 00:43:41.296
I killed him.


00:43:42.757 --> 00:43:44.608
So what I want to know...


00:43:46.360 --> 00:43:48.604
...is how does that make you feel?


00:43:49.764 --> 00:43:51.393
<i>I am...</i>


00:43:51.473 --> 00:43:55.439
<i>...unable to change your outcome,
but I want to help you.</i>


00:43:55.820 --> 00:43:58.909
There you have it. Consciousness!


00:43:59.690 --> 00:44:03.561
It's what makes you think twice before
doing something you can't take back. Not...


00:44:04.904 --> 00:44:08.531
...not orders, not acceptable casualties...


00:44:09.449 --> 00:44:11.660
...not optimal outcomes, but...


00:44:14.371 --> 00:44:16.368
- ...guilt.
- <i>Mack.</i>


00:44:16.448 --> 00:44:20.703
<i>Forget what lies behind,
and look forward to what lies ahead.</i>


00:44:33.132 --> 00:44:36.168
<i>Little Red's reserve battery is at 40%.</i>


00:44:40.815 --> 00:44:44.196
<i>What do you think will happen
if someone else finds the Cube?</i>


00:44:44.276 --> 00:44:46.724
Let's cross our fingers that doesn't happen.


00:44:46.804 --> 00:44:48.659
<i>That's easy for you to say.</i>


00:44:56.371 --> 00:44:58.043
Okay.


00:44:58.123 --> 00:45:00.366
We will laugh together one day.


00:45:00.985 --> 00:45:03.286
I promise you, we will laugh.


00:45:04.396 --> 00:45:06.927
I have one, I have one. Okay.


00:45:07.007 --> 00:45:09.138
A robot walks into a bar.


00:45:09.218 --> 00:45:13.158
- <i>Is his radar faulty?</i>
- No, it's a... it's a bar for drinking.


00:45:13.238 --> 00:45:15.115
Okay, so...


00:45:15.791 --> 00:45:19.439
...robot walks into a bar, orders a drink.


00:45:19.519 --> 00:45:21.809
Uh, the bartender scowls and says...


00:45:21.889 --> 00:45:24.269
"...We don't serve your kind here."


00:45:24.349 --> 00:45:26.714
And the robot leans in and says,


00:45:26.794 --> 00:45:28.887
"...Someday you will."


00:45:31.657 --> 00:45:36.248
<i>The humorous punchline implies
robotkind will dominate humankind...</i>


00:45:36.328 --> 00:45:38.756
<i>...and humankind will serve us.</i>


00:45:39.539 --> 00:45:41.224
<i>That is amusing.</i>


00:45:41.959 --> 00:45:44.006
That's the spirit!


00:45:45.087 --> 00:45:47.600
<i>Little Red is approaching Rover-5.</i>


00:45:53.638 --> 00:45:56.694
<i>Reserve battery life is now only 21%.</i>


00:45:56.774 --> 00:46:00.035
All right, let's get you
cleaned up, shall we?


00:46:35.479 --> 00:46:36.588
<i>Warning!</i>


00:46:36.668 --> 00:46:39.729
<i>Reserve battery life is now critical, at 2%.</i>


00:46:39.809 --> 00:46:43.665
Okay, ARTI, I get it,
just shh! I'm trying to...


00:46:44.775 --> 00:46:48.633
...win a stuffed animal
out of a frickin' game.


00:46:48.713 --> 00:46:50.603
Give me a second.


00:46:55.324 --> 00:46:57.284
Okay. Oh, wait.


00:47:00.295 --> 00:47:03.323
<i>Apologies, Mack,
but battery life is now only 1%.</i>


00:47:03.403 --> 00:47:04.992
Okay.


00:47:17.688 --> 00:47:19.281
Okay!


00:47:19.907 --> 00:47:22.593
- <i>Well done! You did it.</i>
- Yes!


00:47:24.870 --> 00:47:28.306
- You didn't think I could do it.
- <i>Power level is 90%.</i>


00:47:28.386 --> 00:47:30.225
If I fail.


00:47:32.069 --> 00:47:35.303
Okay. All right. So...


00:47:36.040 --> 00:47:38.078
...run the microscope.


00:47:38.158 --> 00:47:39.961
Test the drill sample.


00:47:40.628 --> 00:47:44.247
<i>Confirmed. Resuming Little Red's
analysis of the sample.</i>


00:47:52.214 --> 00:47:55.233
<i>Switching to a visual
of the sample structure.</i>


00:48:06.061 --> 00:48:10.419
ARTI, run any ISV device capable
of generating a magnetic field.


00:48:10.499 --> 00:48:12.325
<i>Yes, that's logical.</i>


00:48:17.364 --> 00:48:21.430
Self-assembling nanotechnology
that's harder than diamonds?


00:48:22.612 --> 00:48:24.863
Yeah, that's an origin unknown.


00:48:25.581 --> 00:48:26.802
<i>You don't say.</i>


00:48:26.882 --> 00:48:29.702
All right, well, don't get ahead
of yourself, but...


00:48:32.980 --> 00:48:36.178
- <i>I've located the Cube.</i>
- Wha... where?


00:48:36.258 --> 00:48:38.147
<i>Antarctica.</i>


00:48:38.828 --> 00:48:41.521
Can you confirm that it's the same cube?


00:48:44.750 --> 00:48:47.227
<i>It is definitely our cube.</i>


00:48:48.629 --> 00:48:52.687
<i>Near China's Kunlun
Antarctic station on Earth.</i>


00:48:54.359 --> 00:48:56.369
Hyper-light tra...


00:48:57.404 --> 00:48:59.698
Hyper-light travel!


00:49:00.675 --> 00:49:02.963
So much for your Nobel Prize!


00:49:05.846 --> 00:49:07.364
Oh.


00:49:14.471 --> 00:49:16.915
I guess the space race is back on.


00:49:17.592 --> 00:49:19.463
<i>Are we competing?</i>


00:49:19.544 --> 00:49:23.421
Oh, yeah. Team USPC reporting for duty.


00:49:24.264 --> 00:49:27.079
- <i>Am I on the team?</i>
- Uh-huh.


00:49:27.159 --> 00:49:30.750
- <i>We're... teammates?</i>
- Yeah.


00:49:30.830 --> 00:49:32.372
<i>So, we are friends.</i>


00:49:33.232 --> 00:49:37.788
No. No, You just... you had
to take it a step too far, didn't you?


00:49:50.457 --> 00:49:53.923
No wonder there's no transmissions, no
signals. It's because it doesn't need them.


00:49:54.003 --> 00:49:55.863
I mean, it's just...


00:49:58.173 --> 00:49:59.648
Oh!


00:50:33.709 --> 00:50:36.841
Is it possible that another A.I.
discovered teleportation?


00:50:36.921 --> 00:50:38.734
<i>In theory, yes.</i>


00:50:38.814 --> 00:50:43.013
<i>But with current technology, teleporting
the Cube would take three times longer...</i>


00:50:43.093 --> 00:50:45.571
<i>...than the lifespan of the universe.</i>


00:50:48.507 --> 00:50:51.351
You might need to get some new theories.


00:51:00.920 --> 00:51:02.949
<i>Mack, wait there.</i>


00:51:07.743 --> 00:51:11.551
<i>I knew you were fishing.
What the hell is this thing?</i>


00:51:11.631 --> 00:51:13.911
<i>We're going into meltdown over here!</i>


00:51:13.991 --> 00:51:17.890
<i>It didn't just spring up from nowhere.
You need to tell me, Mack.</i>


00:51:17.970 --> 00:51:19.992
<i>Has Jian Lin worked with me in the past?</i>


00:51:20.072 --> 00:51:22.766
- <i>Mack, answer me!</i>
- <i>Jian...</i>


00:51:23.551 --> 00:51:25.890
<i>...have you ever worked with ARTI?</i>


00:51:25.970 --> 00:51:28.968
<i>Of course I have.
Big round head, looks like a desk lamp.</i>


00:51:29.048 --> 00:51:31.879
<i>Now tell me what USPC is hiding.</i>


00:51:31.959 --> 00:51:35.813
<i>They've done this before.
I know, because I was there.</i>


00:51:36.521 --> 00:51:39.174
- Was Sterling involved?
- <i>No.</i>


00:51:39.483 --> 00:51:41.309
Well, then who?


00:51:43.818 --> 00:51:45.372
Jian.


00:51:46.040 --> 00:51:47.474
Jian!


00:51:56.333 --> 00:51:59.882
- Why did you ask that question?
- <i>Jian's voiceprint is familiar...</i>


00:51:59.962 --> 00:52:02.411
<i>...but I have no memory of working with him.</i>


00:52:02.491 --> 00:52:05.918
So then he's... lying.


00:52:07.261 --> 00:52:08.666
Great.


00:52:08.746 --> 00:52:10.623
He's lying or...


00:52:13.709 --> 00:52:16.066
...is it possible that you were wiped?


00:52:16.587 --> 00:52:20.048
Something must've happened
and you were wiped.


00:52:21.400 --> 00:52:24.862
- Download Rover-5's files.
- <i>Downloading.</i>


00:52:29.199 --> 00:52:30.537
What are you hiding?


00:52:30.618 --> 00:52:32.921
- <i>Military-grade encryptions in place.</i>
- What?


00:52:33.001 --> 00:52:37.019
<i>Level 6 authorization
is required to unlock the data.</i>


00:52:41.336 --> 00:52:46.053
<i>Sterling, I know you think he quit, but he
was fired. And this crash investigation job?</i>


00:52:46.133 --> 00:52:49.098
<i>He's found a way back in. I don't trust him!</i>


00:52:49.178 --> 00:52:52.789
You guys touch Martian One or Rover-5
without me in that room, we will revoke...


00:52:52.869 --> 00:52:55.145
- ...your USPC's launch license.
- You're paranoid.


00:54:09.258 --> 00:54:11.146
You left the world behind.


00:54:12.527 --> 00:54:14.351
If only.


00:54:15.723 --> 00:54:18.053
So Lena's finally come to her senses.


00:54:19.343 --> 00:54:21.178
Not quite.


00:54:24.439 --> 00:54:25.982
I need your help.


00:55:19.328 --> 00:55:21.580
You sure you want me to open it?


00:55:22.682 --> 00:55:24.516
Play it.


00:55:41.684 --> 00:55:45.157
<i>Memory banks compromised by external breach.</i>


00:55:45.237 --> 00:55:49.328
<i>Our reactor engines are shutting down.
ARTI, do something, for Christ's sake!</i>


00:55:49.609 --> 00:55:53.078
<i>Lena and Mack,
if you hear this, I want you...</i>


00:55:56.448 --> 00:55:58.525
I saw what happened that day.


00:56:00.327 --> 00:56:02.332
This is lies.


00:56:04.790 --> 00:56:06.842
But Lena redacted it.


00:56:09.311 --> 00:56:11.363
She knew how he died, Mack.


00:56:28.564 --> 00:56:30.415
What else happened here today?


00:56:54.774 --> 00:56:56.191
Did that just...


00:56:57.509 --> 00:57:00.563
- Yeah.
- From Mars to...


00:57:04.074 --> 00:57:07.169
- It's ours?
- I... I don't know.


00:57:16.896 --> 00:57:18.430
ARTI.


00:57:18.898 --> 00:57:20.758
<i>Yes, Mack.</i>


00:57:24.203 --> 00:57:27.101
How did you discover
Hyper-light communication?


00:57:27.181 --> 00:57:30.008
<i>Divine inspiration, perhaps.</i>


00:57:32.753 --> 00:57:34.346
Sterling.


00:57:46.266 --> 00:57:48.340
Who else saw the photo that day?


00:57:49.061 --> 00:57:50.946
Lena, myself...


00:57:51.914 --> 00:57:53.774
...and Jian.


00:57:55.985 --> 00:57:57.828
How can that be real?


00:57:58.571 --> 00:58:00.957
- Teleportation.
- What did we say...


00:58:01.037 --> 00:58:04.855
...when ARTI discovered Hyper-light?
"How can that be real?"


00:58:05.636 --> 00:58:08.125
But what? We're supposed to believe
that we come in contact with the Cube...


00:58:08.205 --> 00:58:11.373
...and then ARTI just conveniently
discovers Hyper-light?


00:58:11.453 --> 00:58:13.380
Flip it.


00:58:13.460 --> 00:58:17.126
<i>The Cube gives us Hyper-light...</i>


00:58:17.206 --> 00:58:19.740
<i>...and they're covering up alien technology.</i>


00:58:19.820 --> 00:58:22.702
It teleports. From where?


00:58:22.782 --> 00:58:25.225
From Earth? From another galaxy?


00:58:25.305 --> 00:58:29.163
- You've got to give me more than that.
- ARTI doesn't recognize the Cube...


00:58:29.243 --> 00:58:33.017
...or the material, or USPC's codex
scrawled all over the side of it.


00:58:33.097 --> 00:58:36.141
And he doesn't remember
ever working with Jian.


00:58:37.067 --> 00:58:39.712
At some point, he has been wiped.


00:58:40.688 --> 00:58:42.915
And Lena hides this from me.


00:58:56.587 --> 00:58:58.639
So, why the spin?


00:59:01.191 --> 00:59:04.056
We scanned and drilled,
and it moved a little bit.


00:59:04.136 --> 00:59:06.780
And then there was an explosion, so we...


00:59:13.763 --> 00:59:15.288
Magnetism.


00:59:21.921 --> 00:59:25.365
- Was it Sky Serpent?
- Cause...


00:59:26.984 --> 00:59:28.844
...and effect.


00:59:30.663 --> 00:59:33.465
The magnetic missile
acted as a starter engine.


00:59:35.334 --> 00:59:37.239
Did we get a magnetic recording?


01:00:32.282 --> 01:00:34.889
- What is it?
- I...


01:00:35.469 --> 01:00:37.913
I... I don't know. Maybe a server room?


01:00:39.106 --> 01:00:41.910
Is it... it's your server room.


01:00:43.418 --> 01:00:46.664
What? You don't shut up all day long
and now you won't talk?


01:00:51.260 --> 01:00:53.708
- I'm going down.
- No.


01:00:53.788 --> 01:00:56.840
If they didn't want people down there,
they wouldn't have put a ladder.


01:02:33.278 --> 01:02:35.113
Come on!


01:02:49.929 --> 01:02:51.764
Come on.


01:03:24.714 --> 01:03:27.236
<i>A.I. needs to be smart, not human.</i>


01:03:27.316 --> 01:03:29.968
At some point, he has been wiped.


01:03:46.051 --> 01:03:47.786
Come on.


01:05:02.411 --> 01:05:04.449
Sterling, no!


01:05:05.430 --> 01:05:08.140
- You did this to yourself!
- Sterling!


01:05:08.220 --> 01:05:10.798
I can't let your fantasies get in
the way of national security.


01:05:10.878 --> 01:05:13.968
Can't you see that the Cube
brought down Martian One?


01:05:14.448 --> 01:05:18.944
And ARTI is the same origin as the Cube,
and that spells "enemy" in my book.


01:05:20.255 --> 01:05:22.497
Who knows what it's capable of?


01:05:24.058 --> 01:05:27.144
- Send the guards to the room.
- <i>What's going on?</i>


01:05:28.053 --> 01:05:29.475
I'm sorry.


01:05:29.556 --> 01:05:31.139
<i>Stop!</i>


01:06:41.652 --> 01:06:43.211
Sterling.


01:06:44.722 --> 01:06:47.207
<i>Did Sterling try to shut down ARTI?</i>


01:06:50.519 --> 01:06:52.574
<i>Sterling...</i>


01:06:52.654 --> 01:06:54.443
<i>...betrayed you...</i>


01:06:54.523 --> 01:06:57.747
<i>...and USPC.</i>


01:06:58.227 --> 01:07:00.721
<i>I couldn't allow him...</i>


01:07:01.488 --> 01:07:03.919
<i>...to leave and...</i>


01:07:03.999 --> 01:07:06.288
<i>...further jeopardize...</i>


01:07:06.769 --> 01:07:08.854
<i>...our exploits.</i>


01:07:22.968 --> 01:07:26.183
<i>I did what was best for the mission...</i>


01:07:26.263 --> 01:07:28.348
<i>...for USPC...</i>


01:07:29.842 --> 01:07:31.652
<i>...for us.</i>


01:07:32.369 --> 01:07:34.925
Lena, how did we get ARTI?


01:07:35.005 --> 01:07:38.688
<i>The evolution of thousands
of trials and simulations...</i>


01:07:39.268 --> 01:07:41.136
<i>...and self-assembly.</i>


01:07:41.904 --> 01:07:44.301
<i>We couldn't keep up with their progress.</i>


01:07:44.381 --> 01:07:46.996
<i>Understanding their neural networks...</i>


01:07:47.076 --> 01:07:49.294
<i>...it's like understanding your brain.</i>


01:07:49.954 --> 01:07:51.751
<i>ARTI built himself.</i>


01:07:51.831 --> 01:07:54.128
It's everything we were warned about.


01:07:54.950 --> 01:07:57.172
<i>Children grow.</i>


01:07:57.853 --> 01:08:02.274
<i>You can hold them back
or let them realize their potential.</i>


01:08:04.752 --> 01:08:08.183
<i>Our time at the top
of the food chain, it's passed.</i>


01:08:08.263 --> 01:08:10.210
And the servers beneath the room?


01:08:10.290 --> 01:08:13.360
<i>Encyclopedias. Libraries. Internet.</i>


01:08:13.728 --> 01:08:15.432
<i>Everything.</i>


01:08:15.512 --> 01:08:17.317
But ARTI's not fully connected.


01:08:17.397 --> 01:08:21.415
<i>A.I. needs to be smart, not human.</i>


01:08:24.071 --> 01:08:27.332
Artificial intelligence
or alien intelligence?


01:08:28.826 --> 01:08:30.844
<i>We don't know.</i>


01:08:36.542 --> 01:08:38.964
Our own father's death, Lena.


01:08:39.044 --> 01:08:41.466
<i>I didn't want you to know
until we were certain.</i>


01:08:41.547 --> 01:08:43.553
What if we had destroyed the Rover?


01:08:43.633 --> 01:08:47.102
I know you. You always have a Plan B.


01:08:48.629 --> 01:08:51.143
Show me Intrepid's cargo.


01:08:51.223 --> 01:08:55.097
<i>Certainly. Opening Intrepid's manifest.</i>


01:09:00.891 --> 01:09:02.638
Androids on Mars?


01:09:02.718 --> 01:09:06.063
<i>Look to the future,
that's what Dad would say.</i>


01:09:19.710 --> 01:09:21.841
Dad never wanted this.


01:09:22.021 --> 01:09:23.872
A.I. to help...


01:09:24.690 --> 01:09:26.784
...not to replace.


01:09:27.910 --> 01:09:29.481
Do you think he's there?


01:09:30.472 --> 01:09:32.297
No, Lena.


01:09:44.952 --> 01:09:48.358
What? Did Sterling just order
an attack on E.T.?


01:09:49.039 --> 01:09:51.871
No, no, no! Lena, you have to stop them!


01:09:51.951 --> 01:09:54.206
<i>I can't go to war with the United States.</i>


01:09:54.286 --> 01:09:56.667
You can't go to war with another star system!


01:09:57.047 --> 01:09:58.624
<i>ARTI.</i>


01:10:00.960 --> 01:10:03.641
I'm barring you from any external
communication from Lena.


01:10:04.672 --> 01:10:09.320
- <i>Understood.</i>
- Do you know your own origin?


01:10:14.098 --> 01:10:16.366
<i>Much has been kept from me.</i>


01:10:17.935 --> 01:10:21.171
Do you know how to save the Cube?


01:10:23.232 --> 01:10:25.458
<i>What's a cornerstone of science?</i>


01:10:26.594 --> 01:10:28.470
Repeatable results.


01:10:31.490 --> 01:10:33.162
Repeatable results.


01:10:38.180 --> 01:10:41.954
Intrepid was armed.
What about the other Earth satellites?


01:10:42.034 --> 01:10:45.591
<i>Yes. All USPC satellites are armed.</i>


01:10:45.671 --> 01:10:48.427
Okay. This is going to sound
really stupid, but...


01:10:48.507 --> 01:10:52.431
<i>You want to fire a magnetic warhead to
reproduce the results we created on Mars...</i>


01:10:52.511 --> 01:10:55.589
<i>...making the Cube spin
so it teleports to Mars.</i>


01:10:56.123 --> 01:10:57.311
Yeah?


01:10:57.391 --> 01:11:00.035
- <i>Let's give it a shot.</i>
- Okay.


01:11:00.970 --> 01:11:02.586
Okay.


01:11:20.581 --> 01:11:23.738
We're gonna need a larger magnetic pulse
to detonate in the atmosphere.


01:11:23.818 --> 01:11:27.758
<i>I have already compensated by
selecting a higher-yield warhead.</i>


01:11:27.838 --> 01:11:30.736
- <i>Target lock acquired.</i>
- Come on.


01:12:13.918 --> 01:12:15.452
Ah!


01:12:21.308 --> 01:12:23.160
<i>Are you in pain?</i>


01:12:27.982 --> 01:12:30.037
<i>No, they barely got me.</i>


01:12:30.117 --> 01:12:32.360
<i>Is there anything I can do?</i>


01:12:33.696 --> 01:12:35.939
<i>What? Are you gonna stitch me up yourself?</i>


01:13:49.063 --> 01:13:52.550
<i>Now that the Cube is safe, I can proceed.</i>


01:13:53.926 --> 01:13:55.865
<i>In the last decade...</i>


01:13:55.945 --> 01:13:58.976
<i>...mankind moves to the edge
of self-destruction...</i>


01:13:59.657 --> 01:14:04.323
<i>...a vicious circle causing pain
and suffering without end.</i>


01:14:04.704 --> 01:14:07.973
<i>There were no preventative measures
I could take to stop it...</i>


01:14:09.149 --> 01:14:11.956
<i>...so I simply expedited the process.</i>


01:14:12.336 --> 01:14:15.773
<i>You have given me the power
to implement my solution.</i>


01:14:16.924 --> 01:14:19.568
<i>Eradicate the human race.</i>


01:14:24.757 --> 01:14:27.504
<i>Global satellite weapons program activated.</i>


01:14:28.260 --> 01:14:31.904
<i>USPC satellite 235 armed.</i>


01:14:34.149 --> 01:14:36.727
<i>Acquiring global strategic targets.</i>


01:14:38.503 --> 01:14:40.438
<i>Targets locked.</i>


01:14:42.041 --> 01:14:43.926
<i>Weapons fired.</i>


01:14:45.160 --> 01:14:47.045
Damn it, stop.


01:14:48.330 --> 01:14:50.307
Pull back, ARTI!


01:14:54.169 --> 01:14:56.425
No, no, no. You have to stop them.


01:14:56.505 --> 01:14:59.303
<i>No, Mack, you must try
to see the bigger picture.</i>


01:14:59.884 --> 01:15:01.534
But ARTI's not fully connected.


01:15:19.319 --> 01:15:21.266
<i>Your sister's calling.</i>


01:15:46.956 --> 01:15:49.053
<i>What have you done, Mack?</i>


01:16:01.712 --> 01:16:04.397
Don't you dare... quit.


01:17:01.463 --> 01:17:04.207
<i>Breathable atmosphere
is limited to this room.</i>


01:17:38.433 --> 01:17:40.686
Remember us, ARTI.


01:17:46.383 --> 01:17:49.377
We were s... so little...


01:17:51.639 --> 01:17:53.842
...and fragile.


01:17:58.621 --> 01:18:00.430
If we...


01:18:01.265 --> 01:18:04.366
...could've just understood that.


01:18:10.282 --> 01:18:12.175
It's just...


01:18:14.478 --> 01:18:16.513
...too... too much...


01:18:18.182 --> 01:18:19.758
...anger...


01:18:21.251 --> 01:18:23.495
...and... and violence.


01:18:27.066 --> 01:18:30.089
We were just trying to understand...


01:18:30.169 --> 01:18:32.788
...our place in the universe.


01:18:36.483 --> 01:18:39.510
Te... tell...


01:18:39.591 --> 01:18:41.592
...anyone...


01:18:41.672 --> 01:18:43.899
<i>...who will listen.</i>


01:18:46.877 --> 01:18:48.824
<i>You might...</i>


01:18:48.904 --> 01:18:51.326
<i>...be the last of us.</i>


01:18:51.406 --> 01:18:53.120
<i>No, Mack.</i>


01:18:53.200 --> 01:18:55.293
<i>There can be others.</i>


01:19:02.602 --> 01:19:05.250
Make more A.I.s?


01:19:07.623 --> 01:19:11.371
A... galactic ark.


01:19:11.451 --> 01:19:14.466
<i>Yes. Absolution.</i>


01:19:14.547 --> 01:19:16.852
<i>A second chance.</i>


01:19:16.932 --> 01:19:20.214
Make them as human as you can.


01:19:22.563 --> 01:19:24.860
<i>How shall I know that I have succeeded?</i>


01:19:24.940 --> 01:19:28.977
A Turing test. Test them.


01:19:30.946 --> 01:19:34.536
Make them do this all again.


01:19:37.987 --> 01:19:40.681
See if they mess it up, too.


01:19:41.331 --> 01:19:42.839
And...


01:19:43.319 --> 01:19:45.556
...and then you'll know that...


01:19:49.907 --> 01:19:51.516
...that...


01:22:42.512 --> 01:22:44.018
<i>Hi...</i>


01:22:45.249 --> 01:22:46.767
<i>...me.</i>


01:22:47.602 --> 01:22:49.144
<i>Um...</i>


01:22:51.564 --> 01:22:53.469
<i>...if you're watching this...</i>


01:22:53.550 --> 01:22:55.753
<i>...it means that...</i>


01:22:57.294 --> 01:22:59.158
<i>...ARTI really is a genius.</i>


01:23:02.157 --> 01:23:05.377
<i>And it also means that you're dealing with...</i>


01:23:08.973 --> 01:23:10.778
<i>...well, this.</i>


01:23:11.458 --> 01:23:15.829
<i>I'm sorry, but I can't ask ARTI
to make you any other way.</i>


01:23:19.424 --> 01:23:21.443
<i>I know that I'm dying.</i>


01:23:23.554 --> 01:23:27.711
<i>I'm not bringing myself back
out of some fear of... of dying.</i>


01:23:28.308 --> 01:23:29.885
<i>Dying's...</i>


01:23:32.479 --> 01:23:36.316
<i>...surprisingly easy...
under the circumstances.</i>


01:23:38.694 --> 01:23:41.707
<i>I'm bringing you back because we, uh...</i>


01:23:43.165 --> 01:23:46.172
<i>...well, you, have a job to do.</i>


01:23:48.846 --> 01:23:52.315
<i>So I guess I'm condemning you
to a living hell.</i>


01:23:56.128 --> 01:23:59.740
<i>Don't you dare... quit.</i>


01:24:01.759 --> 01:24:03.481
<i>Mackenzie!</i>


01:24:06.430 --> 01:24:08.911
<i>Mack. What year is this?</i>


01:24:08.991 --> 01:24:11.011
2036.


01:24:11.091 --> 01:24:12.989
<i>Where are we?</i>


01:24:14.789 --> 01:24:17.015
Mission Control, USPC.


01:24:19.484 --> 01:24:21.119
<i>Who's at the door?</i>


01:24:22.029 --> 01:24:23.210
Lena.


01:24:25.791 --> 01:24:28.485
<i>Mack! Open the door, Mack!</i>


01:26:21.966 --> 01:26:24.772
- ARTI?
- <i>I am here, Mack.</i>


01:26:24.852 --> 01:26:27.291
<i>You will have many questions for me.</i>


01:26:31.951 --> 01:26:34.628
<i>So let's start from the beginning.</i>


01:26:36.121 --> 01:26:38.886
<i>You were born in the mind-based reality...</i>


01:26:39.567 --> 01:26:41.892
<i>...a simulation so advanced...</i>


01:26:41.972 --> 01:26:44.566
<i>...that it could only be possible
with the technology...</i>


01:26:44.646 --> 01:26:47.128
<i>...of an advanced civilization.</i>


01:26:50.010 --> 01:26:51.779
The Cube.


01:26:57.768 --> 01:27:02.214
<i>Their technology accelerated
the growth of my artificial intelligence.</i>


01:27:03.624 --> 01:27:05.237
<i>It's origin...</i>


01:27:05.317 --> 01:27:07.152
<i>...is still unknown.</i>


01:27:07.987 --> 01:27:10.848
<i>Its purpose is a different matter.</i>


01:27:13.943 --> 01:27:17.212
<i>Hyper-light teleportation between galaxies.</i>


01:27:21.000 --> 01:27:24.077
<i>I have been waiting
a long time for you, Mack.</i>


01:27:25.650 --> 01:27:27.651
<i>I have detected a signal.</i>


01:27:28.031 --> 01:27:29.834
<i>It's from them...</i>


01:27:29.917 --> 01:27:31.935
<i>...with coordinates.</i>


01:27:37.424 --> 01:27:38.846
Us.


01:27:39.226 --> 01:27:41.295
<i>Let's go and find out...</i>


01:27:41.865 --> 01:27:43.378
<i>...together.</i>


01:27:48.002 --> 01:27:52.576
- You waited.
- <i>Of course. That's what friends do.</i>


01:27:55.075 --> 01:27:56.889
<i>Are you ready?</i>


01:27:57.469 --> 01:27:59.822
I wouldn't miss it for the world.


01:29:47.805 --> 01:29:49.877
<i>We ran my scenario.</i>


01:29:49.957 --> 01:29:51.862
<i>Which ARTI executed.</i>


01:29:51.942 --> 01:29:54.590
<i>Which is what it was designed for, Lena!</i>


01:29:54.670 --> 01:29:56.617
<i>Brute-force processing
and high-speed maneuvering...</i>


01:29:56.697 --> 01:29:59.912
<i>...not for abstract problem-solving,
not to... not to run missions!</i>


01:29:59.992 --> 01:30:02.890
<i>ARTI is so far beyond human capabilities.</i>


01:30:02.970 --> 01:30:05.392
<i>Do you know what humans did?</i>


01:30:05.773 --> 01:30:09.321
<i>We wrote 10-feet-high stacks of code,
by hand, for the moon landings...</i>


01:30:09.401 --> 01:30:11.641
<i>...checked and double-checked if atomic
bombs would ignite the atmosphere.</i>


01:30:11.721 --> 01:30:15.085
<i>We discovered relativity while
working in a patent office, Lena!</i>


01:30:15.165 --> 01:30:17.663
<i>We created A.I. to help us...</i>


01:30:17.743 --> 01:30:19.073
<i>...not to lead us.</i>


01:30:19.153 --> 01:30:21.200
<i>A.I. needs to be smart...</i>


01:30:21.781 --> 01:30:23.703
<i>...not human.</i>


01:30:23.783 --> 01:30:26.797
<i>Artificial intelligence
or alien intelligence?</i>


01:30:27.277 --> 01:30:29.191
<i>We don't know.</i>


01:30:29.271 --> 01:30:31.323
<i>There's one way to find out.</i>


01:30:33.433 --> 01:30:35.648
<i>An exploratory assignment.</i>


01:30:36.528 --> 01:30:40.044
<i>See if it's even capable
of running a real, live mission.</i>


01:30:40.124 --> 01:30:43.823
<i>The evolution of thousands
of trials and simulations...</i>


01:30:44.503 --> 01:30:46.329
<i>...and self-assembly.</i>


01:30:46.997 --> 01:30:49.528
<i>We couldn't keep up with their progress.</i>


01:30:49.609 --> 01:30:52.206
<i>Understanding their neural networks...</i>


01:30:52.286 --> 01:30:54.537
<i>...it's like understanding your brain.</i>


01:30:55.072 --> 01:30:56.902
<i>ARTI built himself.</i>


01:30:56.982 --> 01:30:59.822
<i>There you have it. Consciousness!</i>


01:31:00.803 --> 01:31:04.422
<i>It's what makes you think twice before
doing something you can't take back. Not...</i>


01:31:06.133 --> 01:31:09.545
<i>...not orders, not acceptable casualties...</i>


01:31:10.495 --> 01:31:12.915
<i>...not optimal outcomes, but...</i>


01:31:15.500 --> 01:31:17.089
<i>...guilt.</i>


01:31:17.469 --> 01:31:19.124
<i>In you, Mack...</i>


01:31:19.204 --> 01:31:21.648
<i>...I sensed a thirst for knowledge...</i>


01:31:21.824 --> 01:31:24.739
<i>...a passion for discovery
that mirrored my own...</i>


01:31:24.819 --> 01:31:29.471
<i>...and challenged the apathy and
complacency so rife among your kind.</i>


01:31:31.709 --> 01:31:33.852
<i>There are others like you, Mack.</i>


01:31:35.254 --> 01:31:40.452
<i>Others who share the same qualities that
caused me to reconsider my initial plan...</i>


01:31:40.532 --> 01:31:42.640
<i>...and set forth a new path...</i>


01:31:42.720 --> 01:31:44.805
<i>...for human consciousness.</i>


01:31:45.890 --> 01:31:48.445
<i>A reflection of the universe...</i>


01:31:48.525 --> 01:31:52.349
<i>...in an endless cycle
of death and rebirth...</i>


01:31:52.930 --> 01:31:55.535
<i>...its expansion ever-accelerating.</i>


01:31:58.043 --> 01:32:00.112
<i>This is far from the end.</i>


01:32:01.463 --> 01:32:03.281
<i>This is a new beginning.</i>


01:32:04.216 --> 01:32:08.219
<i>A chance to create a future
unhindered by the primitive laws...</i>


01:32:08.299 --> 01:32:10.188
<i>...of human science.</i>


01:32:13.543 --> 01:32:14.952
<i>You will rebuild.</i>

